  { q: 'What is the Pomodoro Technique?', a: 'The Pomodoro Technique is a focus method created by Francesco Cirillo in the late 1980s. You work in a 25-minute block called a pomodoro, take a 5-minute break, and after four pomodoros take a 15 to 30 minute break. The Best Answer Hub Pomodoro Timer runs this structure with presets and custom intervals.' },
