          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="band">Best Answer Hub</td><td><span class="score lv1">Browser only</span></td><td>None, free, nothing stored</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="band">TomatoTimer</td><td><span class="score lv1">Browser only</span></td><td>None, free</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="band">Pomofocus</td><td>Browser</td><td>Basic timer free; paid Premium tier</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="band">Forest</td><td><span class="score lv3">Installed app</span></td><td>Account; free tier plus paid Plus</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="band">Toggl Track</td><td>Extension plus app</td><td>Sign-up required</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>Alerts do not need an account either: a browser page can raise a system notification and play a sound when the timer ends, with your one-time permission, using the standard web Notifications API (<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Notifications_API" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MDN</a>). That is all a focus timer really needs.</p>

        <div class="cta">
